(  ===================================================================  )
(  STEPPED SHAFT - two diameters, practising roughing with a subroutine )
(  ===================================================================  )
(  Stock  : 14 mm aluminium round, at least 45 mm proud of the collet   )
(  Tools  : T1 right-hand turning, T3 parting blade                     )
(                                                                       )
(          O8              O11             O14                          )
(       +------+        +--------+      +--------+                      )
(       |      |        |        |      |        |   <- collet this end )
(       +------+--------+--------+------+--------+                      )
(         12 mm           12 mm          remainder                      )
(                                                                       )
(  Worth reading as a lesson in ORDER OF OPERATIONS: cut the section    )
(  furthest from the chuck first and take the smallest diameter last,   )
(  so the part stays as stiff as possible for as long as possible.      )
(                                                                       )
(  It also shows a SUBROUTINE. o<rough> takes a target diameter, a Z    )
(  depth and a feed, so the roughing passes are one line each instead   )
(  of four. Run it in the simulator and watch the backplot.             )
(  ===================================================================  )

G21 G18 G40 G90 G95 G7

(  A TRAP WORTH KNOWING: diameter mode G7 applies to G53 machine moves too. )
(  The machine has 48 mm of X travel as a RADIUS, so the fully retracted      )
(  position is X96 in diameter mode, not X48. Writing X48 here would retract  )
(  only half way and leave the turret sitting over the work.                  )
G53 G0 X96

T1 M6
G54
S1400 M3

(  --- face the end --- )
G0 X16 Z1
G1 X-0.4 F0.08
G0 Z1
G0 X16

(  --- rough the O8 section, 0 to -12 mm, in steps on diameter --- )
o<rough> call [12.5] [-12] [0.10]
o<rough> call [11.0] [-12] [0.10]
o<rough> call [9.5]  [-12] [0.10]
o<rough> call [8.4]  [-12] [0.10]

(  --- rough the O11 section, 0 to -24 mm --- )
o<rough> call [12.5] [-24] [0.10]
o<rough> call [11.4] [-24] [0.10]

(  --- finish passes: full depth, slower feed --- )
G0 X11 Z0.5
G1 Z-24 F0.05
G0 X13
G0 Z0.5
G0 X8
G1 Z-12 F0.05
G1 X11.4          ( face the shoulder outward )
G0 X16

(  --- part off at 36 mm --- )
M5
T3 M6
S800 M3
G0 X16 Z-36
G1 X0.5 F0.04
G0 X16

M5
G53 G0 X96 Z0
M30

(  ===================================================================  )
(  One roughing pass: approach clear, cut to depth, retract, return.    )
(    #1 = target diameter    #2 = Z depth    #3 = feed in mm/rev        )
(  ===================================================================  )
o<rough> sub
  G0 X[#1] Z0.5
  G1 Z[#2] F[#3]
  G0 X[#1 + 1]     ( retract before returning, so we never rub the cut )
  G0 Z0.5
o<rough> endsub

